      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nAdd tuned fused-MoE Triton kernel configurations for **NVIDIA A10** covering two Qwen A3B MoE shapes at tensor parallel size 4 in bfloat16:\r\n\r\n- Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B: `E=128` experts, `moe_intermediate_size=768`, so `N=192` per rank at TP=4\r\n  - file: `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/configs/E=128,N=192,device_name=NVIDIA_A10.json`\r\n- Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B: `E=256` experts, `moe_intermediate_size=512`, so `N=128` per rank at TP=4\r\n  - file: `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/configs/E=256,N=128,device_name=NVIDIA_A10.json`\r\n\r\nThere are currently no fused-MoE configs for `NVIDIA_A10` at all, so A10 deployments fall back to the default heuristic config. These two models were chosen because they are popular MoE models that fit on a 4x A10 (96 GB) node in bf16 at TP=4. The `E=256,N=128` shape also has no bf16 config for any device yet.\r\n\r\nI searched open PRs for A10 fused-MoE configs and found none.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nGenerated with the standard tuning script on a 4x A10 24GB host (3 GPUs used as tuning workers; ~1.5 h per model):\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py --model Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B --tp-size 4 --dtype auto --tune\r\npython benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py --model Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B --tp-size 4 --dtype auto --tune\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen compared default vs. tuned kernel time on one A10 with the same script in benchmark mode, pointing the tuned run at the generated files via `VLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER`:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nVLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER=<dir with tuned json> CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1 python benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py --model <model> --tp-size 4 --dtype auto --batch-size 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256 512 1024 2048 4096\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso verified that vLLM loads both checked-in configs from the repo config directory with `get_moe_configs(E, N, dtype=None)` on `NVIDIA A10`.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nEnvironment: vLLM `0.30.1rc1.dev33+g8b660ce96`, torch `2.13.0+cu130`, Triton `3.7.1`, NVIDIA driver `580.126.20`, GPU `NVIDIA A10`.\r\n\r\nKernel time from `benchmark_moe.py` for Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B (bf16, TP=4 shape, one A10):\r\n\r\n| batch size | default config (us) | tuned config (us) | change |\r\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\r\n| 1 | 57.05 | 55.07 | -3.47% |\r\n| 2 | 95.89 | 91.67 | -4.40% |\r\n| 4 | 172.83 | 160.32 | -7.24% |\r\n| 8 | 278.01 | 275.43 | -0.93% |\r\n| 16 | 439.13 | 424.61 | -3.31% |\r\n| 32 | 582.09 | 559.18 | -3.94% |\r\n| 64 | 642.37 | 630.66 | -1.82% |\r\n| 128 | 715.65 | 660.21 | -7.75% |\r\n| 256 | 735.17 | 695.74 | -5.36% |\r\n| 512 | 792.21 | 762.57 | -3.74% |\r\n| 1024 | 1004.36 | 938.03 | -6.60% |\r\n| 2048 | 1416.33 | 1311.07 | -7.43% |\r\n| 4096 | 2417.23 | 2232.51 | -7.64% |\r\n\r\nKernel time from `benchmark_moe.py` for Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B (bf16, TP=4 shape, one A10):\r\n\r\n| batch size | default config (us) | tuned config (us) | change |\r\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\r\n| 1 | 44.13 | 42.05 | -4.71% |\r\n| 2 | 70.18 | 67.59 | -3.69% |\r\n| 4 | 125.09 | 115.95 | -7.31% |\r\n| 8 | 232.46 | 201.27 | -13.42% |\r\n| 16 | 382.15 | 347.36 | -9.10% |\r\n| 32 | 611.75 | 545.48 | -10.83% |\r\n| 64 | 765.10 | 734.30 | -4.03% |\r\n| 128 | 909.79 | 839.38 | -7.74% |\r\n| 256 | 954.34 | 883.63 | -7.41% |\r\n| 512 | 1009.32 | 941.01 | -6.77% |\r\n| 1024 | 1290.08 | 1070.63 | -17.01% |\r\n| 2048 | 1518.99 | 1382.42 | -8.99% |\r\n| 4096 | 2205.58 | 2018.61 | -8.48% |\r\n\r\nThe comparison was run twice; every measured batch size improved in both runs for both models, with run-1 and run-2 change percentages matching closely.\r\n\r\nSanity: both files load with `json.load`, use the tuner batch-size keys and fused-MoE tuning fields, and vLLM logs `Using configuration from .../device_name=NVIDIA_A10.json for MoE layer`.\r\n\r\n## AI assistance\r\n\r\nThis PR was prepared with AI assistance (Claude Code) for running the tuning/benchmarks and drafting this description. I reviewed the config files, the benchmark logs, and every line of this PR.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
